 :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335909/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0296cc2f-3d1f-5bb4-9d36-9b7d30ca6fd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335909/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "207287d5-fe5f-54d4-9e75-b69d3ed6b33c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335909/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-335909/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-335909/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335909/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "2e82ee11-5d98-5ed4-a8c5-74ebd6a85861" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335909/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b7b5179-aec4-5b43-bb47-ed04fb2f4730" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335909/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-335909/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335909" :question/id #uuid "a24f294a-cdfd-53bd-ae89-48540ff56558" :question/math-academy-id "q-335909" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=(4t-8){e}^{t},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment.\n\nThe acceleration is zero at $t=$\n{{field-1}}, and the velocity at this moment is\n$v=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((4t-8){e}^{t}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{t}+(4t-8){e}^{t} \\\\  & =(4t-4){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((4t-4){e}^{t}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{t}+(4t-4){e}^{t} \\\\  & =4t\\,{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4t\\,{e}^{t} & =0 \\\\ 4t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t=0.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\nv(0)=(4\\cdot 0-4){e}^{0}=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is zero at $t=0,$ and the velocity at this moment is $v=-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-335909/field-1" "q-335909/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bee6d4bf-79da-5eb3-a214-8c045dbce5bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335909"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-315553/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "c1910bb6-f3cf-5171-b2b6-2daa5437a3cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-315553/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d549997-b084-581c-bda3-216acfa1d1be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-315553/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-315553/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-315553/field-2/4df5abd760fcc0c1f12fd39bed941f36f7fc1293827512782ff053149dd1f7ec" :answer/id #uuid "3c2b4319-bc98-5712-ad7c-66778fb352f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-315553/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd9cab1d-818b-5061-bc3b-f16d37e13237" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-315553/field-2/4df5abd760fcc0c1f12fd39bed941f36f7fc1293827512782ff053149dd1f7ec" :answer-field/choices ["q-315553/field-2/4df5abd760fcc0c1f12fd39bed941f36f7fc1293827512782ff053149dd1f7ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-315553" :question/id #uuid "dd05cb61-1025-52d9-8f80-565c0086f261" :question/math-academy-id "q-315553" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=(5t-15){e}^{t},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment.\n\nThe acceleration is zero at $t=$\n{{field-1}}, and the velocity at this moment is\n$v=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((5t-15){e}^{t}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{t}+(5t-15){e}^{t} \\\\  & =(5t-10){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((5t-10){e}^{t}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{t}+(5t-10){e}^{t} \\\\  & =(5t-5){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5t-5){e}^{t} & =0 \\\\ 5t-5 & =0 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t=1.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\nv(1)=(5\\cdot 1-10){e}^{1}=-5e.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is zero at $t=1,$ and the velocity at this moment is $v=-5e.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-315553/field-1" "q-315553/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bee6d4bf-79da-5eb3-a214-8c045dbce5bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-315553"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335910/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "4f886dff-b205-5a0c-b8d8-e2edbc2cfbec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335910/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "215e29b1-6f54-59d1-9463-12f9d17a5e42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335910/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3c809dfb-dc43-5522-9c20-cc65e1d2cf6d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335910/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-335910/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-335910/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335910/field-2/16bebe09fbd5a8bcf95ea3b50d19881f6449ce43315cad3d9ae5f8fea910a7ce" :answer/id #uuid "a048d998-d5e4-5142-9c40-5f93f051b56c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{e^4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335910/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c75eb0f-c41d-5aa7-9cb7-c74f7154be79" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335910/field-2/16bebe09fbd5a8bcf95ea3b50d19881f6449ce43315cad3d9ae5f8fea910a7ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-335910/field-2/16bebe09fbd5a8bcf95ea3b50d19881f6449ce43315cad3d9ae5f8fea910a7ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335910" :question/id #uuid "a437f4ef-d65f-59fa-b5ea-a9457558efc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-335910" :question/problem "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=(3t-6){e}^{-t},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment.\n\nThe acceleration is zero at $t=$\n{{field-1}}, and the velocity at this moment is\n$v=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((3t-6){e}^{-t}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{-t}+(3t-6)(-{e}^{-t}) \\\\  & =(9-3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((9-3t){e}^{-t}) \\\\  & =(-3){e}^{-t}+(9-3t)(-{e}^{-t}) \\\\  & =(3t-12){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3t-12){e}^{-t} & =0 \\\\ 3t-12 & =0 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t=4.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\nv(4)=(9-3\\cdot 4){e}^{-4}=-3{e}^{-4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is zero at $t=4,$ and the velocity at this moment is $v=-3{e}^{-4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-335910/field-1" "q-335910/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bee6d4bf-79da-5eb3-a214-8c045dbce5bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335910"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
